Yes! Finally I made it!

I have played Nethack now and then for many years (playing for a few weeks
then wait to next year). I have had the impression that the game was
impossible to beat. When I saw that version 3.4.2 was out I started to play
again and this time I got some character as far as the quest and thought it
may be possible to win. I played random classes to find one that I was good
with, monks were quite successful. Lately I have played some wizards most
for fun because I was very bad at them. Most died early, I think only one
ever saw the Oracle until...

Yariaria the neutral human Evoker started out like all his predecessors by
just roaming the dungeon trying to find some cool stuff. But unlike the
others he found a polymorph trap and (cough) accidentally displaced his 2
pets (he had tamed another one) into the trap. One became a winter wolf and
the other a lich. Wow, liches are cool Yariaria thought and went on. The
lich took care of everything that came in their way. The winter wolf was
lost in a trap hole and was found much later still peaceful.
My memory from this part of the game are not so good (didn't take any notes)
so the order of things might be wrong.
Anyway, Yariaria found and cleared a throne room and got a wish. The CoMR
was burnt and he had an oilskin cloak so he wished for +2 GDSM which got his
AC below zero. Maybe SDSM would have been better but, hey, the grey worked
to the end.
He found two general stores and the lich took out the keepers. with spell of
id he didn't need them anyhow. An aligned altar got the two companions busy
for a while. Got magicbane and some spellbooks and the castle tune. Then the
first big mistake: killed a 'd' on the altar and #offered, turned out to be
an werewolf! Not good!
Yariaria continued down and eventually found another aligned altar. Some
sacrificing later Thoth was pleased again. Some more sacrificing and
Yariaria was crowned Envoy of Balance and received his well deserved
spellbook of finger of death. Did some polypiling but I can't remember what
he got, a cornuthaum and a "oLS at least I guess.
Went all the way to medusa (killing her with a mirror) then turned around
and did sokoban. The price was BoH and that was well needed. With some
advices from r.g.r.n Yariaria decided to dump the arch-lich there and
continue to the gnomish mines.
In minetown the priest (chaotic iirc) gave him 6 points of protection for
all his money. Then the second big mistake, I don't know why but I made
Yariaria quaff from a sink and he turned into a grey dragon. Walking around
in the town and using his breath to kill monsters he accidentally hit the
priest. Forced back into his normal form he tried to kill the priest before
he killed him. The priest won!
You die...
But wait...
Your medallion begins to glow!
Then the priest went down. The oilskin cloak was destroyed when Yariaria
changed form so he gladly put on the robe the priest left and continued to
mines end where he got the luckstone. Next stop: the quest. Nothing much to
say there. The Dark One was given the finger. Got a wish from the throne on
the home level and used it for gauntlets of dexterity.
Next came some loot managing. Moved all stuff to main stash on dlvl 21.
He then decided to pay Croesus a visit. There was a mind flayer there so to
be on the safe side Yariaria said goodbye to all 'h'. With a ring of
conflict the fort was easy. Made a tin out of Croesus (but forgot it in the
stash before the ascension). Mayor polypiling followed. He got gauntlets of
power (never used), Hawaiian shirt, "oLS and some more useful stuff.
Back at the stash he fireproofed and enchanted all armor.
Opened the drawbridge with a magic flute but it got destroyed by a wand of
striking so he had to use his ww-boots. Cleared the castle but got no wish
from the throne, the wand had 2 charges though. Used them for ring of
levitation (he had no other source of levitation) and magic marker.
Yariaria now prepared for Gehennom. With all armor enchanted he had AC -42
(nice number).
The valley was easy with conflict. The first encounter with a named demon
was a bit scary. Yariaria found it best to hit Asmodeus with a potion of
paralysis so he didn't teleport away while he cast magic missile on him.
(Why can he teleport on a no-teleport level, its not fair). Juiblex made
Yariaria really sic by swallowing him but he solved that one with a wand of
teleport and the spell of cure sickness. Then Juiblex was kill from a
distance with magic missile. Baalzebub teleported to the stairs but Yariaria
went after him and found him just standing there while taking round after
round of missiles. Orcus went upstairs but there he was beaten to the next
stairs so Yariaria could easily take him out.
Then followed a lot of digging paths though numerous mazes until Yariaria
hit a level that was to hard to dig holes in. There he found a place that
vibrated and marked it (with a carrot, that was gone when he came back but
he remembered the place).
He then visited Vlad in his tower, used the finger of death and took the
candelabrum. After repacking at his stash and wishing for 7 candles (there
were enough in minetown but he had found a brand new WoW with 3 charges)
Yariaria ran down to Rodney. The tower was no problem, he fingered the
Wizard and took the book (turn ~46800)
Performed the invocation about 200 turns later. The sanctum was easy with
conflict. Fingered the high priest and took the amulet and named it REAL.
Yariaria now ran for his life up and up. The force hit him 6 times (38->40,
38->38, 37->37, 36->37, 33->34, 34->35). He left Gehennom about 1000 turns
after taking the amulet.
All went smooth. He stopped to pick up his collection of gems, refresh some
spells and drop unneeded stuff (he left his ~100000 zorkmids in the stash).
Rodney showed up on dlvl 4 and got the finger directly.
Being paranoid Yariaria double checked the amulet before taking the final
stairs.
Fingered the Wizard on the first turn on the plane of earth. Used a crystal
ball to find the portal. Used some wands of digging to get there. Then an
Archon showed up just before Yariaria stepped into the portal and it
summoned nasties. He fought until he could walk into the portal. The Archon
followed.
The plane of air had a bad start. The Archon summoned lots of monsters and
blinded Yariaria all the time (he didn't have ESP). His HP was reduced under
100 when he decided to change from "oR to "oLS. With a combination of
conflict and luck he managed to get away from the Archon and find the
portal.
The plane of fire was a vacation compared to air. He killed only one
salamander and left the level with full HP and Pw.
On water he decided that he should use a scroll of genocide to remove all
';'. Rodney made his last appearance and got the same treatment as the other
times.
Yariaria arrived on astral plane a bit to the right so he started to go that
way. Found an arch-lich and decided a wish for a blessed scroll of genocide
or two (but got one) was a good use for that wand he had. No more 'L' (he
felt sorry for his pet lich that was left in sokoban).
Famine guarded that altar and got the finger 4 times on the way there. The
priests made it easy with all the insects they summoned and an Angle read a
scroll of create monster while confused filling the space outside the temple
with blobs. The altar was Ptah's. Fingered Famine one last time on the way
out before a giant was very kind and blocked the path behind Yariaria with a
boulder.
Center altar next. Guarded by death. He killed him 3 times before he
realised he was at the wrong altar again. Killed death once more on the way
out.
Yariaria fingered Pestilence once on the way to the left temple. Didn't
bother to kill many Angels and priests just ran past them where possible.

